of dysphagia, contributing significantly to the healthcare landscape in Madrid.", "SENPE:SENPE, or Sociedad Española de Nutrición Clínica y Metabolismo, is a prominent Spanish society dedicated to the fields of clinical nutrition and metabolism. This professional organization plays a crucial role in addressing hospital malnutrition in Spain, providing essential documentation and management strategies. SENPE collaborates with SEMICYUC to develop updated recommendations for critical care nutrition, ensuring that healthcare professionals have access to the latest guidelines for nutritional support.\n\nIn addition to its focus on clinical nutrition, SENPE is actively involved in standardizing practices related to pediatric enteral nutrition. The organization works on creating consensus documents that outline best practices and guidelines for pediatric nutrition, thereby enhancing the quality of care for young patients. SENPE also engages in discussions and provides guidelines related to enteral nutrition and diet therapy, further solidifying its role as a key player in the nutritional landscape of Spain.\n\nMoreover, SENPE is recognized as the Spanish Society of Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition, emphasizing its commitment to nutritional care in hospital settings. This includes the development of guidelines and consensus documents that inform nutritional practices for both parenteral and enteral nutrition. The society also supports scientific initiatives, such as the publication on oropharyngeal dysphagia, highlighting its dedication to advancing knowledge and practices in the field of nutrition.\n\nOverall, SENPE serves as a vital resource for healthcare professionals in Spain, promoting best practices in clinical nutrition, pediatric nutrition, and nutritional support in various healthcare settings.", "AEHH:AEHH, or Asociación Española de Hostelería, is a Spanish association focused on the hospitality sector. It is also known as the Asociación Española de Hostelería Hospitalaria, which is a scientific society that supports research and knowledge dissemination related to oropharyngeal dysphagia. This dual identity highlights AEHH's commitment to both the hospitality industry and the medical field, particularly in addressing issues related to swallowing disorders.", "SEEN:SEEN, or Sociedad Española de Endocrinología y Nutrición, is a prominent Spanish society dedicated to the fields of endocrinology and nutrition. This organization plays a crucial role in the study and treatment of endocrine and nutritional disorders, contributing significantly to the development of clinical guidelines and evidence-based practices. SEEN is involved in various aspects of clinical nutrition, including the publication of texts and resources that support professionals in the field. \n\nThe society is particularly focused on issues related to obesity and diabetes, engaging in clinical trials and research that enhance understanding and treatment of these conditions. SEEN also provides educational resources, including materials related to dysphagia, and endorses scientific literature, such as the book on oropharyngeal dysphagia. With a commitment to advancing knowledge and practice in endocrinology and nutrition, SEEN supports education and research initiatives, making it a vital organization in the health landscape of Spain.", "ADENYD:ADENYD, or the Asociación de Enfermeras de Nutrición y Dietética, is a scientific society based in Spain that focuses on the fields of nutrition and dietetics. The organization is dedicated to supporting various initiatives, including the production of a book on oropharyngeal dysphagia. It serves as a professional association for nurses who specialize in nutrition and dietetics, promoting best practices and advancements in these areas.", "GUÍAMÉDICA FORMACIÓN EN SALUD:guíamédica formación en salud is an organization that provides health training and resources.", "VEGENAT HEALTHCARE:Vegenat HEALTHCARE is an organization involved in healthcare solutions, as indicated by its logo in the document.", "DISFAGIA OROFARÍNGEA:Disfagia orofaríngea (DOF), or oropharyngeal dysphagia, is a medical condition characterized by difficulty in swallowing, which can significantly impact a patient's nutrition and quality of life. This condition often necessitates dietary adaptations in texture and viscosity to ensure safe swallowing, as well as specific care strategies during feeding to prevent complications such as aspiration pneumonia, malnutrition, and dehydration. \n\nDisfagia orofaríngea is commonly observed in patients with various medical conditions, including stroke, and it requires a multidisciplinary approach for effective assessment, rehabilitation, and management. Healthcare professionals utilize various diagnostic tests, such as pH-impedance and manometry, to evaluate the severity of the condition. Early detection and treatment are crucial, as untreated DOF can lead to serious health consequences.\n\nThe management of oropharyngeal dysphagia involves not only dietary modifications but also rehabilitation techniques and specific nursing care to ensure safe oral feeding. It is relevant in hospital settings, particularly in food service and preparation, where understanding the dietary needs of affected patients is essential. Additionally, the condition is the focus of various health data collection and management systems, highlighting its significance in clinical practice and research.\n\nOverall, oropharyngeal dysphagia is a complex swallowing disorder that requires comprehensive care strategies to enhance patient outcomes and maintain nutritional health.", "GRUPO AULA MÉDICA, S.L.:Grupo Aula Médica, S.L. is the publishing house responsible for the edition of the book on oropharyngeal dysphagia.", "JULIA ÁLVAREZ HERNÁNDEZ:Julia Álvarez Hernández is a prominent medical professional specializing in endocrinology and nutrition, serving as the Head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Section at the Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias in Alcalá de Henares, Madrid. In her role, she is actively involved in the management and treatment of patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia, working within the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofaríngea. Julia is also a co-author and coordinator of a book discussing oropharyngeal dysphagia, contributing her expertise to the section that addresses this condition. Her work encompasses a broad range of topics related to nutrition and dysphagia, highlighting her commitment to advancing knowledge and treatment in these fields.", "ESPAÑA:España es un país europeo que ha sido el escenario de importantes investigaciones y programas relacionados con la salud y la nutrición. Uno de los estudios más destacados es el Proyecto PREDIMED, un ensayo clínico que investiga la dieta mediterránea y su impacto en la salud cardiovascular. Sin embargo, España enfrenta desafíos significativos en términos de salud pública, como el aumento de la obesidad, que ha duplicado su tasa en los últimos 20 años, superando actualmente el 20% de la población.\n\nEn el ámbito de la nutrición, se ha observado una prevalencia de nutrición parenteral en adultos de 5,06 pacientes por millón de habitantes. Además, se han realizado estudios sobre la prevalencia de enfermedades respiratorias como la EPOC y las bronquiectasias, reportando cifras significativas de casos por cada 10,000 habitantes. En cuanto a la cirugía bariátrica, España lleva a cabo técnicas como el bypass gástrico y la gastrectomía vertical laparoscópica para tratar la obesidad.\n\nEl país también regula la autonomía del paciente y sus derechos en relación con la información y documentación clínica, incluyendo decisiones sobre nutrición artificial. A nivel demográfico, España tiene un 18.2% de su población mayor de 65 años, cifra que se proyecta aumentará al 24.9% para 2029 y al 38.7% para 2064.\n\nEn el ámbito de la salud digital, España se está convirtiendo en un actor clave, especialmente en el tratamiento de la disfagia. Sin embargo, el país enfrenta dificultades para cumplir con las recomendaciones internacionales sobre la ingesta de grasas saturadas, que actualmente superan el 10%. Aproximadamente el 10% de la población adulta padece algún grado de enfermedad renal crónica, y la litiasis biliar es la causa más común de pancreatitis aguda, especialmente entre mujeres de mediana edad.\n\nEn cuanto a la diabetes, cerca de 30,000 menores de 15 años sufren de Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 1, y se han reportado tasas significativas de trastornos alimentarios. Los estudios también indican que la población consume niveles de omega-3 cercanos a los recomendados, aunque presenta una alta relación omega-6 a omega-3. La dieta mediterránea ha demostrado beneficios significativos para la salud, especialmente en la salud cardiovascular.\n\nLa ingesta promedio de potasio en España es de", "DISFAGIA:Dysphagia is a medical condition characterized by difficulty in swallowing, affecting individuals across various age groups and often associated with a range of underlying health issues, including neurological disorders, head and neck tumors, and esophageal conditions. This condition can manifest as challenges in swallowing both solid and liquid foods, leading to significant nutritional risks, complications such as aspiration, and potential malnutrition. \n\nDysphagia is prevalent in approximately 3% of the general population and is particularly common among patients with specific medical conditions, such as stroke, multiple sclerosis, and esophageal cancer. It can severely impact a patient's quality of life and dietary choices, necessitating specialized dietary modifications and interventions by healthcare professionals. \n\nManagement of dysphagia often requires a multidisciplinary approach, including nutritional assessment, the use of thickeners, and enteral nutrition in more severe cases. The condition is also gaining attention in the context of digital health solutions, highlighting the need for effective assessment and treatment strategies. \n\nOverall, dysphagia is a complex condition that requires careful evaluation and tailored interventions to ensure safe swallowing and adequate nutritional intake, making it a critical focus in both clinical practice and research.", "AULAMEDICA FORMACION EN SALUD:", "UNIDAD FUNCIONAL DE DISFAGIA OROFARÍNGEA:The Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofaríngea (UFDOF) is a specialized, multidisciplinary unit established in 2013 within the Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias (HUPA). Its primary focus is on the assessment, diagnosis, and treatment of patients suffering from oropharyngeal dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. The unit aims to provide comprehensive care through collaborative efforts among various healthcare professionals, ensuring that patients receive tailored and effective management for their swallowing disorders. UFDOF emphasizes quality care and integrates multiple disciplines to enhance the treatment and rehabilitation processes for individuals with dysphagia, thereby improving their adapted nutrition and overall well-being.", "VEGENAT® HEALTHCARE:Vegenat® Healthcare is a company that provided unconditional support for the creation of the book on oropharyngeal dysphagia.", "JAVIER COELLO:Javier Coello is the editor who worked on the book, contributing to its production and ensuring its timely release."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}